WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.500
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing the top 50 devilish

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.980
details you missed in Lucifer's final season,
from ingenious easter eggs and call-backs

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.759
to hilarious meta references and hidden jokes.

00:00:12.759 --> 00:00:15.389
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:18.000
Since she first stole the hearts of Lucifans
in the pilot,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.200
My name's Beatrice, but everybody calls me
Trixie.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.200
That's a hooker's name.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.200
What's a hooker?

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.200
Ask your mother.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.930
Scarlett Estevez has gifted us some wonderful
scenes, and there's some fun easter eggs at

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:31.090
Maze's wedding to memorable moments between
her and Trixie.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:35.039
So when Maze walks down the aisle, as she
reaches her little friend they do a fist bump

00:00:35.039 --> 00:00:39.329
then their signature cut-throat sign which
we saw a longer version of in the third season

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:41.670
episode Mr and Mrs Mazikeen Smith.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:46.640
Later at the reception, as Adam and Dr Linda
walk into the scene, watch the background

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.519
very carefully as while Eve is enjoying a
glass of something sparkly, Maze is pouring

00:00:51.519 --> 00:00:55.670
something a little stronger;
after which she checks around and surreptitiously

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:58.730
tries to pass the glass of hard liquor to
Trixie!

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:02.809
Until, that is, Eve realizes what her new
wife's up to and stops her!

00:01:02.809 --> 00:01:06.939
But this isn't the first time that Maze has
offered Trixie an alcoholic drink, as she

00:01:06.939 --> 00:01:10.630
also did that as a bartender at Lux in Season
1.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.680
Is this a Shirley Temple?

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.680
Sure.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:18.570
Check out the pile of presents at the reception,
and among the boxes you'll spot a spiky gift

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.520
with a festive white bow attached!

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.600
As one of Hell's foremost torturers, Mazikeen
certainly knows her weaponry, and will doubtless

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:29.880
appreciate this addition to her collection
especially as this particular weapon is called

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.049
a morning star.

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:35.659
Of course, it's at the wedding that Ella reveals
she knows her friends' celestial secret.

00:01:35.659 --> 00:01:39.770
And for Lucifans, the apocalypse board she
created to work it all out is the gift that

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:41.420
just keeps giving for Lucifans!

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:45.299
For example, there's her theories about what
caused Dan the frog to fall from the sky,

00:01:45.299 --> 00:01:49.840
which include whether it's some kind of weird
side effect from Detective Dan's favourite

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:50.840
dessert.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:56.000
The red eyes post-it note on Luci's photo
is a nod to his devil eyes which he used briefly

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.469
in Season 3 on Ella's brother, who could well
have told her at some point likely leading

00:02:00.469 --> 00:02:01.920
her to this clue.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:06.060
And proving what a great detective mind she
has, we can see she figured out everyone's

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:10.050
secret including Charlie being half angel
and Maze a demon.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:13.980
That picture of Maze by the way is from the
hilarious time in Season 5 she dressed up

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.590
and tried to imitate Ella to make herself
more emotionally available.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:20.159
Oh, my God, I have that exact same shirt!

00:02:20.159 --> 00:02:21.159
Yes, you did!

00:02:21.159 --> 00:02:22.159
Wait.

00:02:22.159 --> 00:02:23.159
Did you steal my clothes?

00:02:23.159 --> 00:02:28.260
As for Dan, it seems Ella briefly entertained
ideas that he was also a supernatural creature

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:32.049
like a werewolf, vampire or centaur but ended
up dismissing them.

00:02:32.049 --> 00:02:36.830
Funny for many reasons including that actor
Kevin Alejandro starred in the vampire TV

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:40.650
show True Blood;
and also Goddess, who Dan dated, has centaurs

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.290
in her new universe!

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:46.430
The feather in the bag is a reference to the
Season 5 finale where the writers had some

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:50.220
fun with us making it seem Ella was about
to discover the truth:

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.270
I think I know what this is about, Lucifer.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:53.270
You, you do?

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:55.140
So tell me the truth.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.799
You hit an emu with your car, didn't you?

00:02:56.799 --> 00:03:00.879
By the way, fun fact:
when Season 5 was going to be the final season,

00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:05.500
the plan was for Ella to discover the truth
right at the very end in the closing montage

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:09.120
where she was babysitting Charlie and he sprouted
wings.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:13.480
And I love that, along with the many wild
headlines and apocalyptic Post-It Notes, Ella's

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:16.980
also written what looks like a rather more
mundane reminder to herself:

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:18.770
"Did you turn off stove?"

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:23.430
Lucifer's eclectic To-Do List is a funny insight
into his mind.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:27.740
He's already decided against becoming God
and manages to bond with his daughter Rory,

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:32.420
and up there next is checking in on Father
Frank from the Season 1 fan favourite episode,

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.420
A Priest Walks Into A Bar.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.280
It makes sense Luci would want to visit him
in Heaven and see what he's up to, given how

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.030
hard he took his death.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:43.800
Father Frank was one of the few people to
realise that Lucifer was actually the Devil

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.670
and he reminded Luci that God had not abandoned
him:

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:47.930
You're wrong, Lucifer.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:49.190
Remember...
your father...

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:50.560
has-has a plan.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:55.239
It's also hard not to chuckle at Luci's idea
to mess with Dan by naming him after Casper

00:03:55.239 --> 00:04:00.610
the Friendly Ghost as well as his plan to
rewatch all twelve seasons of Bones, that's

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:03.730
246 episodes, thank you very much!

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:06.469
That show was the perfect combination of procedure
and banter.

00:04:06.469 --> 00:04:10.660
As for São Paolo's inclusion on the list,
that might be a reference to the real-life

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:15.290
serial killer imprisoned in the Brazilian
city who calls himself Lucifer and has apparently

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:19.079
killed many other prison inmates he views
as bad people.

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:23.390
Perhaps Luci intends to put a stop to someone
using his name for their own ends, as he did

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:26.810
with Luci-phony, the Lucifer impersonator
from Season 1.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.440
I'm Lucifer freaking Morningstar!

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:29.440
Oh...

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:32.530
Are you now?
we can't have you running around cheapening

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:34.389
the Lucifer brand, now, can we?

00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:38.870
Because, as we know, one thing Lucifer hates
in particular is being used as a scapegoat

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:41.471
for the bad and evil choices human beings
make by themselves.

00:04:41.471 --> 00:04:43.990
The Devil made me do it.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:46.630
I have never made any one of them do anything.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:51.250
And, of course, given this is Lucifer's list
there's a final reference to a new sexual

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.130
position he wants to try out.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:58.740
A billboard for the TV series ¡Diablo! based
on Lucifer's original Season 1 poster pops

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:00.930
up in the episode 'Buckets of Baggage'.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:05.310
And that ad first appeared during a magnificently
meta Season 5 murder investigation.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:07.890
You want to find the killer, figure out their
yearning.

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:09.680
Isn't there a better word for that?

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:13.740
And interestingly enough, the deliberate choice
to insert the ¡Diablo! billboard into this

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:18.670
particular aerial shot of Sunset Boulevard
means it's juxtaposed with a real-life Catholic

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:21.259
billboard that plays on both the US "Got Milk?"

00:05:21.259 --> 00:05:25.160
campaign and the Biblical miracle of water
being turned into wine.

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:29.150
And also in this shot is a real-life strip
club whose name, "Seventh Veil", is a nod

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:33.610
to the Dance of the Seven Veils performed
by Salomé to get King Herod to execute John

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:35.110
the Baptist.

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:38.310
When Lucifer ponders what to wear to visit
Jimmy Barnes...

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:39.310
Now which do you prefer?

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.310
The iconic white or pomegranate for more of
an "original sin" vibe?

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:47.740
...he seems to confirm the theory of some
scholars that pomegranates, not apples, were

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.020
the fruit that tempted Adam and Eve in the
Garden of Eden.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:54.880
The red seeded fruit has been a running theme
in the show appearing prominently in paintings

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:59.009
at Charlotte the Goddess's law office and
getting a shout-out as one of original God's

00:05:59.009 --> 00:06:00.349
mysterious creations.

00:06:00.349 --> 00:06:03.590
He does inexplicable things from time to time.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.930
Marsupials, pomegranates, the gall bladder.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:08.410
And during Lucifer's investigation of Jimmy's
Hell Loop,

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:12.690
they take a period tour back to the 80s where
playing at the movie theatre is "Althea: Queen

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:15.539
of the Quarks", one of Penelope Decker's best-known
movies.

00:06:15.539 --> 00:06:20.170
Posters for the film have appeared previously
on the show and it was also mentioned in Season

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:21.170
5.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:22.170
Miss Decker, I'm a huge fan.

00:06:22.170 --> 00:06:24.370
Althea: Queen of the Quarks, that should have
won you an Oscar.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:28.280
While Chloe's mum doesn't appear in the final
season, Luci mentions that Trixie's staying

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:31.930
with her in the opening episode:
Grandma Penelope's heart's grown three times

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:33.840
the size thanks to her time with Trixie.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:38.199
That's a reference to The Grinch, whose heart
triples in size after he learns the true meaning

00:06:38.199 --> 00:06:41.949
of Christmas in particular thanks to a little
girl called Cindy Lou Who.

00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:46.910
And it's also a nod to Scarlett Estevez, who
plays Trixie, and her role in Illumination's

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:49.699
animated Grinch movie as one of Cindy Lou's
friends.

00:06:49.699 --> 00:06:55.020
There are several hat-tips this season to
the 1990s romantic thriller Ghost, from Maze's

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:59.030
reaction to ghost-Dan asking her to give Ella
a message:

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:03.050
No, I did not traipse over here on my wedding
night to be your Whoopi Goldberg.

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:06.500
...to Luci and Chloe's Unchained Melody moment
in the panic room.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:11.410
And there's even a cameo from Patrick Swayze's
brother Don who pops up as a gas station owner

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.690
during Luci's search for his daughter.

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:17.139
Hat-tip to Raghu for pointing that out on
my last video!

00:07:17.139 --> 00:07:21.390
When the Morningstar family ends up on Dr
Linda's couch with a case of future child

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:26.180
angst, the symmetry of Lucifer and Rory's
body language not only reflects how much they

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:28.729
have in common,
She takes after you in her exits.

00:07:28.729 --> 00:07:33.280
but it also mirrors the Season 5 scene where
Luci and God had their own therapy session

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:34.710
with the good doctor.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:39.970
Speaking of similarities, both Rory and God
also seem less than impressed with Luci's

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:43.600
large alcohol collection:
nothing is ever good enough for you.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:45.759
Why's your kitchen just a wall of Scotch?

00:07:45.759 --> 00:07:49.220
An entire wall of liquor upstairs and it's
all just whiskey?

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:54.159
And both Luci and Rory's Devil Faces pop up
when their respective fathers are under threat.

00:07:54.159 --> 00:07:57.349
Plus, they also have very similar tastes in
TV!

00:07:57.349 --> 00:08:00.180
the best TV show you have ever seen.

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:01.180
Bones.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.710
The spin-off from my time kicks your Bones'
ass.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:06.590
More Bones is the perfect combination of procedure
and banter.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:10.550
So, in many ways the apple really hasn't fallen
far from the tree!

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:14.509
Luci's love affair with Bones actually began
back in Season 3:

00:08:14.509 --> 00:08:16.050
Watched all 12 seasons.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:17.050
It's riveting stuff.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:18.500
It's like watching a documentary of us.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:23.460
And in Season 6, he's still not over it getting
the chop at Fox, the same channel that also

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:26.220
cancelled Lucifer!
this is a terrible idea.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.379
Worst I've heard since some genius decided
to cancel Bones.

00:08:29.379 --> 00:08:35.040
In fact, in episode 5, Luci thinks he disappears
from Rory's life due to death by dentist as

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.910
Dr Kyle seems strangely familiar to him.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:42.450
But then he realises why:
Do these commercials ever run during Bones?

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:45.090
Syndicated audiences are tooth decay audiences.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:49.810
Which reminds me of another time when Luci's
Bones obsession led him astray in Season 3:

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:51.680
Detective, I've seen that man before.

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:52.910
He's the killer.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:57.710
That man turned out to be an actor from Bones
in both real life and in Lucifer!

00:08:57.710 --> 00:09:02.220
On top of all those tributes to the former
Fox show, Bones actress Patricia Belcher also

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:04.390
guest stars in Season 6 as Loretta.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:09.610
I love the song choice of 'Worship' by the
artist LACES for Eve and Maze's wedding, and

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:14.350
the way that episode's editor has cut the
action to the song lyrics is just fantastic,

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:18.840
as it gives us moments like the camera focusing
on Lucifer and Chloe as the words 'maybe in

00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:22.710
another life' ring out, foreshadowing their
separation by the end of the show and their

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:24.430
eventual reunion in Hell.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:28.060
Then there's the shot of Maze with the lyrics
'Cause Heaven won't take me';

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:32.410
then we cut to Eve on the line 'Devil won't
take me', which certainly fits her Season

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:36.360
4 experience with Lucifer;
then we move to Luci and Chloe again as LACES

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:41.420
sings 'Nothing feels better than you'; before
cutting to ghost-Dan, followed by Amenadiel,

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:44.350
on the line 'If angels won't save me'.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:48.730
Given Eve's Garden of Eden origins, it feels
especially appropriate that she and Maze are

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:53.290
married in front of a large tree and a pair
of flower-covered rings, in their own little

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:54.840
paradise of sorts.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:58.900
The real-life location for the wedding is
the lush garden of the Walt Disney Concert

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:02.420
Hall in LA,
which seems extra fitting as Inbar Lavi plays

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:06.910
the original sinner Eve with all the excitement
and innocent wonder of a Disney princess with

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:08.630
an added naughty side.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:13.200
The garden theme continues at the reception,
with Maze and Eve sitting in front of a heart-shaped

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:18.130
tree covered in pinky red fairy lights, a
colour associated with both love and the devil,

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:22.460
and it also reminds me of classic images of
the Tree of Knowledge.

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:26.280
Another delightful little detail, you could
say even that it's the icing on the cake,

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:31.270
is the cake topper which is actually a mini-version
of Eve and Maze, dressed in the very same

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:33.530
outfits they got married in!

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:38.630
Maze's choice of gifts for kids has certainly
stayed consistent over the seasons, with new-born

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:43.330
Rory getting a cutting-edge present from the
demon, just as baby Charlie and Trixie did

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:44.440
in Season 4.

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:46.980
Maze, you know she's not allowed to play with
knives.

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:49.350
Relax, Dan, these knives aren't for Trixie.

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:50.580
They're for a baby.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:55.310
And talking of Charlie, at his birthday party,
there's a big present wrapped in serpent-covered

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:58.610
paper, a hint perhaps that it's from his uncle
Lucifer.

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:03.130
And Charlie getting his wings on his second
birthday fits nicely with the fact he's entering

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:06.560
the "Terrible Twos",
the period of development when toddlers often

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:11.000
experience temper tantrums as they test their
boundaries and want greater independence.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:15.790
While Amenadiel's pleased as punch, Linda
looks shocked, as after all he'd told her

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:18.730
in Season 5 their son wouldn't be getting
wings at all.

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:21.940
Do you not realize that this is good news?

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:23.540
No more ugly-ass bubble wrap.

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:25.990
No more worrying about a head-on with a 737.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:29.930
And at the polar opposite end of the gift-giving
spectrum to Maze is Ella.

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:33.790
And what else would you expect as a present
from Miss Lopez than something you could give

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:36.170
a nice big old hug to, like a teddy bear.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:39.670
There is, of course, a lot more to discuss
about that ending and whether it was a good

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:44.650
way to finish the series which I go into in
full detail in my ending explained video.

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:47.950
Tap here to watch that or follow the link
in the video description.

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:50.920
So, what were your favourite moments in the
final season?

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:53.760
And what other details or easter eggs did
you spot?

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:55.940
Let me know in the comments below.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:59.770
And if you enjoyed this, then a thumbs-up
and a share are hugely appreciated.

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:03.640
Tap left to check out my next Lucifer video
or tap right for something else you're sure

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:04.640
to like.

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:06.520
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:07.480
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

